OL,3,GNEWSAThames Water grateful as use falls
OL,4,Aafter hosepipe ban
OL,5,
OL,6,FThames Water has said it is "grateful"
OL,7,Fto residents after household water
OL,8,Fdemand across its region fell by 6%
OL,9,Ffollowing the introduction of a
OL,10,Fhosepipe ban.
OL,12,FThe ban, which came into force on 23
OL,13,FJuly, affects the company's 10.1
OL,14,Fmillion customers and means hosepipes
OL,15,Fshould not be used to water gardens,
OL,16,Fclean cars, fill paddling pools or
OL,17,Fswimming pools, or clean windows.
OL,19,FThe company's water director Martin
OL,20,FPadley said demand in the Thames Valley
OL,21,Fremained high and that customers should
OL,22,F"continue using only what they need".
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
